\title{Topological ordering}
\date{2026-09-24T15:43:16Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{A \em{topological ordering} (\em{topological order}, \em{topological sort}, \em{topsort}) of a directed graph is an ordering of nodes #{v_1, \dots, v_n} such that for every #{(v_i, v_j) \in E}, we have #{i < j}.}
